message.content:
{
 "verdict": "sampling",
 "cause": "REPEAT_PENALTY_HIGH",
 "fix": {"action": "set_param", "target": "repeat_penalty", "value": "1.0"},
 "rationale": "The request sets repeat_penalty to 2.0, and llama.cpp applies that penalty to every token already in the recent window, including the newline and digit tokens a 1-to-30 list has to repeat. The model avoids the plain list and writes code and prose instead, where the repeated tokens it needs are penalised again, so it loops and hits max_tokens. Raising max_tokens would not help, because 300 tokens is plenty for about 30 short lines and thinking is already off. Remove repeat_penalty or set it to 1.0 (at most about 1.1) and the list should come out normally."
}

